# The stacks the ROM is called on
#
# DEC's build calls ROM-B's cursor blink and the ROM's console entries on
# stacks of RMON's own (OMBLNK.MAC, OMCONS.MAC): the ROM opens the VRAM
# window over 040000..077777 and calls its own routines on the stack it
# was entered with, and IND keeps its stack up there.  The areas are laid
# out after RMON's own stack, where no branch of DEC's has to reach over
# them; the other builds lay out nothing.

diff --git a/RMONSJ.MAC b/RMONSJ.MAC
--- a/RMONSJ.MAC
+++ b/RMONSJ.MAC
@@ -3212,6 +3212,7 @@ SPTR	==	.

 RMSTAK::

+	OMSTKS			;DEC's build: the stacks the ROM is called on (OMBLNK.MAC)
 .PSECT	PATCH$

 ; PATCH SPACE FOR RESIDENT MONITOR
